derivations.claim:
For a regular face parametrization, the differential maps a coordinate vector $z$ to $Df z$ and its squared Euclidean length is $z^TG_fz$. The vector $G_f^{-1}
abla(u\circ f)$ is therefore the coordinate vector whose image under $Df$ has the defining inner products with every tangent vector; its image is the tangential gradient. Taking its squared norm gives $
abla(u\circ f)^TG_f^{-1}
abla(u\circ f)$. The Gram determinant gives the $k$-volume scaling factor.

